WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:04.932
- So this house is perfect
for viewing the Olympics.

00:00:04.932 --> 00:00:06.893
It's 10 minutes from the stadium.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.690
- [Jennifer] Tracey
Northcott was expecting

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:11.030
this Airbnb listing

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:14.570
to bring in more than
$30,000 during the Olympics.

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.230
- We've got two TVs you can sit down

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:17.160
and watch the Olympics.

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:18.268
That was the idea.

00:00:18.268 --> 00:00:20.880
- [Jennifer] But the Games
in Tokyo are underway

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:23.160
and her ambitious plan
to rent out this home

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:26.300
and about 20 others during
the event has been a bust.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.630
- My properties are completely empty.

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:30.200
Nothing, zero.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.870
- [Jennifer] A ban of
foreign spectators due

00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:34.800
to the pandemic has taken
a toll on reservations.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.600
Around 34,000 nights in Tokyo

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.820
have been booked on
Airbnb during the Games.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:41.700
Just compare that to the
200,000 nights booked in Rio

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:44.170
during the 2016 Olympics.

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:46.130
- [Narrator] Airbnb is proud to partner

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:48.930
with the Olympic and Paralympic games.

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:50.160
- [Jennifer] And that's
also a disappointment

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:53.090
for Airbnb, which made a
big bet on the Olympics

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:56.304
when it became the Games'
official accommodation partner.

00:00:56.304 --> 00:00:57.233
- Airbnb was anticipating

00:00:57.233 --> 00:00:58.730
that this would give them really

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:01.520
some major brand
credibility and awareness.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:02.580
- [Jennifer] Airbnb is hoping

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:03.950
that its sponsorship investment

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:06.373
will still pay off during
future Olympic events.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:09.920
For hosts who are fully
independent from the app,

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:11.760
the priority is paring losses,

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:13.830
and the Tokyo Games are
highlighting the risks

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:16.333
of investing heavily in
short-term accommodation.

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:20.210
Northcott moved to Japan

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:22.230
from Australia more than 20 years ago

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:23.790
as a software engineer.

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:24.870
In the past few years,

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:27.280
using her own funds and
taking out a mortgage,

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:29.860
she became a full-time Airbnb host.

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:33.667
- This house, it's a lovely
classic Japanese home.

00:01:33.667 --> 00:01:36.670
- [Jennifer] It's not easy
being an Airbnb host in Japan.

00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:38.680
The country has some of
the strictest regulations

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:40.240
on short-term rentals in the world,

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:43.040
according to hospitality
industry analysts.

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:46.240
To host guests, Northcott had
to set up a proper company,

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:48.960
pay $2,000 in licensing fees per house,

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:51.410
and outfit some places
with professional alarms

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:54.303
and safety systems similar
to the ones used in hotels.

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:57.040
She was expecting a surge in demand

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:58.370
during the Tokyo Olympics,

00:01:58.370 --> 00:02:00.250
similar to the one of the Rio Games

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:04.580
when Airbnb listings' revenues
increase by about 2,500%,

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:06.660
compared with regular times.

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:08.770
- By the end of 2019, we
were completely booked.

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:13.343
We were planning on making
around about 500,000 US dollars.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:15.860
- [Jennifer] Analysts
say increasing the number

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:17.300
of Airbnb accommodations

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:19.460
can actually help cities like Tokyo

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:21.020
to avoid building too many hotels

00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:22.880
in preparation for the Games.

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:24.640
- Airbnb is an interesting proposition

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:26.580
for something like the Olympics.

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:28.470
- [Jennifer] Makarand Mody
studies the hospitality industry

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:29.880
at Boston University.

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:32.530
- The Olympics in general
have been called into question

00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:33.750
by many destinations

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.010
just because of the amount of money

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:37.980
and infrastructure that
is typically required

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:39.760
to host the Olympics.

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:41.210
- [Jennifer] New hotels and accommodations

00:02:41.210 --> 00:02:43.290
are usually built leading up to the Games.

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:46.040
And Mody says Airbnb
provides another option,

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:48.410
used homes that are already available.

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:51.527
- With Airbnb, you don't really
have to create accommodation

00:02:51.527 --> 00:02:54.030
that will then just remain unused

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:55.980
after the Olympics are done.

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:58.080
- [Jennifer] Now studies
say the city has a surplus

00:02:58.080 --> 00:02:59.790
of Airbnb listings.

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:01.870
- We were just waking up every morning

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:05.740
to cancellation after
cancellation after cancellation.

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:07.990
- [Jennifer] To help hosts
cover cancellation costs due

00:03:07.990 --> 00:03:09.100
to the pandemic,

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:13.360
Airbnb committed more than $250
million globally last year.

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:15.390
In Tokyo, Northcott says she received

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:16.440
a couple thousand dollars

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:18.450
through Airbnb schemes.

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:19.390
- It would have been nice

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:21.604
to have had more support from Airbnb.

00:03:21.604 --> 00:03:23.730
- [Jennifer] So for her
business to survive,

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:24.830
she had to pivot.

00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:27.430
First, she targeted
different types of customers,

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:28.580
people who had to self-isolate

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:29.730
because they had traveled

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:32.080
or had been in contact
with a COVID patient.

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:33.270
- This is the cleaning area.

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:36.832
We've kept everything based
on the CDC guidelines.

00:03:36.832 --> 00:03:39.460
There's alcohol, there's bleach.

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:41.000
- [Jennifer] She also
marketed her properties

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.230
to locals looking for staycations.

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:44.690
We've got a ton of DVDs.

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:46.440
Then if you wanted to work,

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:48.690
we put together a desk

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:52.000
that has a nice window, fast Wi-Fi.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.900
- [Jennifer] Northcott says
this has helped her pay some

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.460
of the bills but she had to look

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:57.780
for long-term renters, broke leases,

00:03:57.780 --> 00:03:59.520
and eventually got rid of 15 homes

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:02.270
because she couldn't afford
the rent on the properties.

00:04:02.270 --> 00:04:03.960
They did send me a nice shirt though.

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:08.610
But that's really been about
the only contact I've had

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:11.510
with Airbnb regarding the Olympics.

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:13.980
- [Jennifer] The company
specifies in its terms of service

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:15.780
that hosts operate independently

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:18.349
and have complete discretion
over their listings.

00:04:18.349 --> 00:04:20.170
- [Narrator] Helping host cities,

00:04:20.170 --> 00:04:22.630
athletes and local communities.

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:24.200
- [Jennifer] Airbnb
still sees the Olympics

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:25.950
as a big business opportunity.

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:27.660
It has run a number of associated ads

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:28.963
and marketing campaigns.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:33.030
- Your logo as a brand is
potentially all over the stadiums

00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:36.000
and all over the other Olympic
co-branding opportunities.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.020
So I think that's a big public relations

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:39.410
and an advertising play.

00:04:39.410 --> 00:04:40.570
- [Jennifer] One of the biggest plays

00:04:40.570 --> 00:04:42.480
is a series of digital experiences

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:45.000
with Olympic athletes
through the platform.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:47.180
Users can sign up to hear stories directly

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:48.540
from their favorite athletes,

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:50.750
or get personal tips
on a training routine.

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:53.860
- Now, to do something with
character and integrity,

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:55.868
it's not an overnight success.

00:04:55.868 --> 00:04:58.480
- [Jennifer] Mody says this
kind of unique experience

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:00.400
builds a softer image of Airbnb,

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:02.100
which could help when dealing with locals

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:04.940
and regulators in markets
that have been tough to crack.

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:06.570
- [Makarand] The credibility that you gain

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:08.680
from something like the
Olympics helps you make

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:11.393
that push when you're lobbying government.

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:14.640
- [Jennifer] And Airbnb is
in this for the long run

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:15.580
since its partnership

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:19.010
with the International Olympic
Committee runs until 2028.

00:05:19.010 --> 00:05:22.020
So Mody says the strategy will
play out not only in Tokyo

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:25.720
but also the next Games
in Beijing and Paris.

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:27.860
- In Paris where the
mayor is really trying

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:31.270
to curb Airbnb, Airbnb's going to use this

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:33.750
and say look, you may
wanna be a little better

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:35.910
towards us because we're gonna make sure

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:38.560
that you don't have an oversupply.

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:39.716
- [Jennifer] In terms of visibility,

00:05:39.716 --> 00:05:41.320
Airbnb may still benefit

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:43.000
from its massive marketing opportunity

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:44.520
at the Tokyo Olympics.

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:45.970
Hosts like Northcott say they're trying

00:05:45.970 --> 00:05:47.310
to get through the pandemic

00:05:47.310 --> 00:05:49.930
and hope to revive their
business in the future.

00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:51.860
- I'm a migrant, I choose to live here,

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:54.750
and I want to be able to show other people

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:56.260
why it's such a great place to live.

00:05:56.260 --> 00:05:58.150
So I'm gonna keep giving it life support

00:05:58.150 --> 00:05:59.200
for as long as I can.

